---
import Code from './Code.astro';
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
import { links } from '../data/links';
---

<section class="section" id="setup" aria-labelledby="setup-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="section-head" data-reveal>
      <h2 id="setup-title">Set up in three&nbsp;steps.</h2>
      <p>Once. Each step is in the Settings window too, with the text ready to copy.</p>
    </header>

    <ol class="steps" role="list">
      <li class="step" data-reveal>
        <span class="step-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
        <h3>Add a read-only token</h3>
        <p>
          In the Hetzner Cloud Console, under <b>Security → API tokens → Generate</b>, with <b>Read</b> permission.
          One per project. Rackbar tries it before it keeps it.
        </p>
        <a class="link" href={links.console}>Open the Hetzner Console <Icon name="external" size={14} /></a>
      </li>

      <li class="step" data-reveal>
        <span class="step-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
        <h3>Pick <code>~/.ssh/hcloud</code></h3>
        <p>Create a folder of its own inside <code>~/.ssh</code> and choose it in Settings → SSH. It is the only folder Rackbar can see.</p>
        <Code code="mkdir ~/.ssh/hcloud" label="the mkdir command" />
      </li>

      <li class="step" data-reveal>
        <span class="step-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
        <h3>Add two lines to <code>~/.ssh/config</code></h3>
        <p>At the end, once. Your own <code>Host</code> blocks above them still win.</p>
        <Code code={'Match all\nInclude hcloud/config'} label="the two lines for ~/.ssh/config" />
        <p class="small">Or append them from a terminal:</p>
        <Code code={"printf '\\nMatch all\\nInclude hcloud/config\\n' >> ~/.ssh/config"} label="the printf command" />
      </li>
    </ol>

    <p class="note-zsh" data-reveal>
      No completions in zsh? Its completion system is off in the stock macOS <code>~/.zshrc</code>. Add
      <code>autoload -Uz compinit &amp;&amp; compinit</code>, before plugins such as zsh-syntax-highlighting.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
